{
  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: 2 days of lower abdominal (below umbilicus / suprapubic) aching with nausea and feeling hot/sweaty.\n- Symptoms (onset/duration/severity/aggravating/alleviating): Symptoms began ~2–3 days ago, gradual onset, constant dull suprapubic ache causing nausea; feels hot/sweaty (subjective fever); no vomiting. Urinary frequency increased (no dysuria, no urgency, no foul smell). Had constipation about 1 week ago which has resolved; normal bowel movements since yesterday. Reports a little pink discoloration in urine or possibly spotting for the last couple of days and expects her period soon.\n- Past medical history: No chronic medical problems reported.\n- Medications / Allergies: No regular medications. Uses Implanon (etonogestrel) implant for contraception. Allergic to amoxicillin.\n- Family / social history: Lives with boyfriend, sexually active with one partner. Brother has type 1 diabetes. Non-smoker.\n- Vital signs / exam findings: None recorded in transcript; patient reports feeling hot/sweaty but denies light-headedness or fainting.\n- Labs / imaging: None performed/not mentioned. Clinician advised face-to-face exam and pregnancy test.\n- Other relevant negatives: No vaginal discharge, no severe localized unilateral pelvic pain, no vomiting, no syncope, no known fever measurement, no urinary pain or stinging.",
