    "V": [
      "Ovarian torsion: Torsion causes acute pelvic pain from vascular compromise of an adnexal structure — could present with lower abdominal pain and nausea. (Transcript: lower abdominal pain and nausea). Less likely given non-severe/dull and non‑sudden onset, but included because torsion is time-sensitive."
    ],
    "I": [
      "Urinary tract infection / acute cystitis: Suprapubic pain, increased urinary frequency and possible haematuria/’pink’ urine support cystitis. Feverish sensations and nausea can occur with more systemic involvement.",
