      "Pregnancy-related (including threatened miscarriage or ectopic pregnancy): Irregular bleeding/spotting, lower abdominal pain and nausea require pregnancy to be excluded. Ectopic pregnancy can present with abdominal pain and spotting and is potentially life‑threatening — clinician specifically recommended pregnancy testing."
    ]
  },
